    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Verifies that when decode() is called one byte at a time, the codec correctly buffers the first hex nibble in ibitWorkArea (stored as value+1 to distinguish from the empty-value 0) and only emits a decoded byte once both nibbles of a hex pair have been received. The optimization path is triggered when exactly one hex character is available in the current call and there is no previously buffered nibble, so the codec defers allocation and output until the second nibble arrives."
   },
   {
